),Bcoef(a3,E),s), where s(j)=z(j)/E(j)−z(j⊖1)/E(j⊖1) for every j∈ℕ.\n\n12. integrate_from_zero [K]. For every r0∈K, s:ℕ→K and j∈ℕ, define I(r0,s,j)=withInitial(r0+s(1),s,j). Expanding the supplied definition gives r0+Σ_{k<j+1}s(k)−s(0), equivalently r0 plus the sum over 1≤k≤j.\n\n13. integrate_initial [K]. For every r0∈K and s:ℕ→K, I(r0,s,0)=r0, I(r0,s,1)=r0+s(1), and I(r0,s,2)=r0+s(1)+s(2), as a conjunction of all three equalities.\n\n14. integrate_increment [K]. For every r0∈K, s:ℕ→K and j∈ℕ, I(r0,s,j+1)−I(r0,s,j)=s(j+1).\n\n15. reduction_reconstruction [K]. For all a1,a2,a3,E:ℕ→K, assume Sol3(a1,a2,a3,E) and E(j)≠0 for every j∈ℕ. For every s:ℕ→K satisfying Sol2(Acoef(a2,a3,E),Bcoef(a3,E),s), and every r0∈K, set zI(j)=E(j)I(r0,s,j) for all j∈ℕ. The conclusion is the conjunction of Sol3(a1,a2,a3,zI), zI(0)=E(0)r0, and, for every j∈ℕ, zI(j+1)/E(j+1)−zI(j)/E(j)=s(j+1).\n\n16. p. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and j∈ℕ, p(ε,c,j)=PEven(c,j) if ε=0, and POdd(c,j) otherwise.\n\n17. q. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and j∈ℕ, q(ε,c,j)=QEven(c,j) if ε=0, and QOdd(c,j) otherwise.\n\n18. r. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and j∈ℕ, r(ε,c,j)=REven(c,j) if ε=0, and ROdd(c,j) otherwise. In definitions 16–18, the branch test is equality to zero, not parity modulo two.\n\n19. theta. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and j∈ℕ, let e=cast_ℚ(ε) and J=cast_ℚ(j). Define θ(ε,c,j)=c/[2(J−1)(2J+2e−1)].\n\n20. factorial_step. For every ε,j∈ℕ, define S_ε(j)=(2J+e)(2J+e−1)∈ℚ, where J and e are the rational casts of j and ε.\n\n21. factorial_weight. For every ε,j∈ℕ, define F_ε(j)=cast_ℚ((2j+ε)!).\n\n22. factorial_weight_ne_zero. For every ε,j∈ℕ, F_ε(j)≠0.\n\n23. factorial_weight_succ. For every ε,n∈ℕ, F_ε(n+1)=S_ε(n+1)F_ε(n).\n\n24. factorial_step_ne_zero. For every ε,n∈ℕ, S_ε(n+1)≠0.\n\n25. parity_coefficient_factors. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, and every n∈ℕ, put j=n+3. The conclusion is the conjunction of p(ε,c,j)/(cS_ε(j))=2+θ(ε,c,j), q(ε,c,j)/(S_ε(j)S_ε(j⊖1))=1+2θ(ε,c,j), and cr(ε,c,j)/(S_ε(j)S_ε(j⊖1)S_ε(j⊖2))=θ(ε,c,j).\n\n26. scale_factor. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and j∈ℕ, define W_ε,c(j)=c^j/F_ε(j).\n\n27. scaled_sequence. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ, μ:ℕ→ℚ and j∈ℕ, define V_ε,c,μ(j)=W_ε,c(j)μ(j).\n\n28. moment_solution. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and μ:ℕ→ℚ, define M(ε,c,μ) to mean that for every n∈ℕ,\nc²μ(n+3)=p(ε,c,n+3)μ(n+2)−q(ε,c,n+3)μ(n+1)+r(ε,c,n+3)μ(n).\n\n29. scale_factor_ne_zero. For every ε∈ℕ and every implicitly bound c∈ℚ, if c≠0, then W_ε,c(j)≠0 for every j∈ℕ.\n\n30. scale_factor_succ. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and n∈ℕ, W_ε,c(n+1)=(c/S_ε(n+1))W_ε,c(n).\n\n31. conjugate_solution_iff [K]. For every a1,a2,a3,w,z:ℕ→K, assume w(j)≠0 for every j∈ℕ. Then Sol3(a1,a2,a3,z) if and only if Sol3(b1,b2,b3,y), where, for every j∈ℕ, b1(j)=w(j)a1(j)/w(j⊖1), b2(j)=w(j)a2(j)/w(j⊖2), b3(j)=w(j)a3(j)/w(j⊖3), and y(j)=w(j)z(j).\n\n32. scaled_coefficients. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, and every n∈ℕ, put j=n+3 and W=W_ε,c. The conclusion is the conjunction of W(j)(p(ε,c,j)/c²)/W(j⊖1)=2+θ(ε,c,j), W(j)((−q(ε,c,j))/c²)/W(j⊖2)=−(1+2θ(ε,c,j)), and W(j)(r(ε,c,j)/c²)/W(j⊖3)=θ(ε,c,j).\n\n33. moment_iff_normalized. For every ε∈ℕ, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, and every μ:ℕ→ℚ, M(ε,c,μ) if and only if Sol3(j↦p(ε,c,j)/c², j↦−q(ε,c,j)/c², j↦r(ε,c,j)/c², μ).\n\n34. moment_iff_scaled. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, and every μ:ℕ→ℚ, M(ε,c,μ) if and only if Sol3(j↦2+θ(ε,c,j), j↦−(1+2θ(ε,c,j)), j↦θ(ε,c,j), V_ε,c,μ).\n\n35. moment_iff_second_difference. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, and every μ:ℕ→ℚ, M(ε,c,μ) if and only if, for every n∈ℕ, Δ²V_ε,c,μ(n+1)=θ(ε,c,n+3)Δ²V_ε,c,μ(n).\n\n36. difference_weight. For every ε∈ℕ, c∈ℚ and n∈ℕ, define D_ε,c(n)=(cast_ℚ(n)+2)W_ε,c(n+2).\n\n37. difference_weight_ne_zero. For every ε∈ℕ, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, and every n∈ℕ, D_ε,c(n)≠0.\n\n38. difference_weight_recurrence. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, every c∈ℚ and every n∈ℕ, D_ε,c(n+1)=θ(ε,c,n+3)D_ε,c(n). There is no c≠0 hypothesis.\n\n39. moment_difference_formula. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, and every μ:ℕ→ℚ satisfying M(ε,c,μ), the following holds for every n∈ℕ: Δ²V_ε,c,μ(n)=(Δ²V_ε,c,μ(0)/D_ε,c(0))D_ε,c(n).\n\n40. moment_finite_reconstruction. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, every c∈ℚ with c≠0, every μ:ℕ→ℚ satisfying M(ε,c,μ), and every n∈ℕ, put V=V_ε,c,μ and D=D_ε,c. Then V(n)=V(0)+(V(1)−V(0))cast_ℚ(n)+Σ_{i<n}Σ_{k<i}[(Δ²V(0)/D(0))D(k)].\n\n41. affine_moment. For every ε∈ℕ, c,A,B∈ℚ and j∈ℕ, define H_ε,c,A,B(j)=(F_ε(j)/c^j)(A+B·cast_ℚ(j)).\n\n42. scaled_affine_moment. For every ε∈ℕ and c,A,B∈ℚ, if c≠0, then V_ε,c,H_ε,c,A,B equals the function j↦A+B·cast_ℚ(j), as equality of functions ℕ→ℚ.\n\n43. affine_moment_solution. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, and every c,A,B∈ℚ with c≠0, M(ε,c,H_ε,c,A,B).\n\n44. normalized_solution_with_zero_term. For every ε∈ℕ with ε=0 or ε=1, and every c∈ℚ with c≠0, let H=H_ε,c,1,−1/3. The conclusion is the conjunction M(ε,c,H), H(0)=1, and H(3)=0.\n\n45. table_ratio. For every a,b,cc,d,j∈ℚ, define T(a,b,cc,d,j)=(j²+aj+b)/(j²+cc·j+d).\n\n46. table_cancellation. For every τ,j∈ℚ, assume j≠0 and j+τ≠0. Then T(τ+1/2,τ/2,τ,0,j)=1+1/(2j).\n\n47. missed_table_parameter. For every j∈ℕ with 1≤j, T(−1/4,−3/8,−3/4,0,cast_ℚ(j))=1+1/(2cast_ℚ(j)).\n\n48. missed_table_not_in_old_branches. With no variable binders, this is the conjunction of the rational inequalities (|2(−3/4)+1|−1)/4≠−3/8 and −((−3/4)+1)/2≠−3/8.\n\n49. legendre2 [K]. For every x∈K, define L2(x)=(3x²−1)/2.\n\n50. legendre3 [K]. For every x∈K, define L3(x)=(5x³−3x)/2.\n\n51. low_mode_representative_differences [K]. For every x,a,b∈K, the conjunction holds: L2(x)/a−(L2(x)−1)/a=1/a, and L3(x)/b−(L3(x)−x)/b=x/b.\n\n52. low_mode_difference_nonzero [K]. For every a,b∈K, assume a≠0 and b≠0. Then L2(0)/a≠(L2(0)−1)/a and L3(1)/b≠(L3(1)−1)/b.\n\n53. a4. For every c∈ℚ, define a4(c)=1+15/c.\n\n54. a6. For every c∈ℚ, define a6(c)=1+105/c+945/c².\n\n55. coefficient_step. For every n∈ℕ and c,an,am∈ℚ, with U=cast_ℚ(n), define coefficient_step(n,c,an,am)=(1+(4U²−1)/c)an+((2U+1)/(2U−3))(an−am).\n\n56. remainder_coefficients_from_initials. For every c∈ℚ, coefficient_step(2,c,1,1)=a4(c) and coefficient_step(4,c,a4(c),1)=a6(c).\n\n57. remainder_identity. For every c∈ℚ, a6(c)−(63/c)a4(c)=1+42/c.\n\n58. remainder_unbounded_on_reciprocals. For every M∈ℚ and N∈ℕ, there exists n∈ℕ such that N<n, 0<1/(cast_ℚ(n)+1), and M<a6(1/(cast_ℚ(n)+1))−[63/(1/(cast_ℚ(n)+1))]a4(1/(cast_ℚ(n)+1)). All three conditions are conjuncts. The existential index is natural, and M need not be positive.\n\n59. even_z_plus. For every j∈ℕ, define Zplus(j)=muEvenPlus(1,j)/[(cast_ℚ(j!))²4^j], equivalently cast_ℚ((2j+1)!)/[(cast_ℚ(j!))²4^j].\n\n60. even_z_minus. For every j∈ℕ, define Zminus(j)=muEvenMinus(1,j)/[(cast_ℚ(j!))²4^j], equivalently cast_ℚ((2j)!)/[(cast_ℚ(j!))²4^j].\n\n61. example_ratio_difference. For every j∈ℕ, define d(j)=Zminus(j)/Zplus(j)−Zminus(j⊖1)/Zplus(j⊖1).\n\n62. printed_reduction_residual. This is a rational constant with no arguments, defined by Rprint=a2Even(1,3)Zplus(1)(d(3)+d(2))+a3Even(1,3)Zplus(0)(d(3)+d(2)+d(1))−Zplus(3)d(3).\n\n63. printed_reduction_counterexample. With no variable binders, the declaration states the rational equality Rprint=69/224.\n\n64. corrected_reduction_same_data. With no variable binders, the declaration states the rational equality Zplus(3)d(3)+(a2Even(1,3)Zplus(1)+a3Even(1,3)Zplus(0))d(2)+a3Even(1,3)Zplus(0)d(1)=0."
